osts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:39:53-07:00","id":158301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/151040-ooc-wyoming-in-the-dusk-hunter-mortal-game?p=158281#post158281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a few questions relating to my character's skills and merits. Now, Eulalia has three dots in Professional Training. The 1-dot version says to take two dots in Contacts relating to her field. I'm pretty sure that's a merit, so do I add that merit on top of all the others? 3-dot says I get a third asset skill(easy enough) and I can also take two specialties in all three, so can I add those six specialties on top of the automatic 3 I get, or would I use up those 3 for the asset skills?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you can add that Merit on top of the others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for the specialties, you pick two new specialties to add to your sheet, in any of the asset skills you have. Make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis",